# The vendored AAS metamodel schemas are third-party bytes whose integrity is
# recorded as a SHA-256 in their NOTICE.md. Line-ending translation would change
# those bytes on disk without changing the blob, so the recorded hash would fail
# to verify on any checkout that normalises — which is the default on Windows.
# Keep them byte-exact so the provenance record stays checkable.
#
# A glob rather than one line per revision: a schema added without its pin is
# exactly the case where the omission goes unnoticed, because the hash only
# fails on someone else's machine.
crates/dpp-tests/fixtures/aas/aas-*.json -text
